From d4af5abf4e709ac4185751ecd057c6820d9867ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:35:06 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_screenlocker: one Form page with Locking / Manual Lock /
 Appearance, appearance config loaded after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form, with the existing Appearance sub-page (docs/page-design.md 1, 2). kscreenlockerrc keys (Daemon/*, Greeter/*),
the org.kde.screensaver configure call, the global shortcut and the lock screen / wallpaper plugin config are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- "Configure Appearance…" was a toolbar action only; it is now a button in an "Appearance" section at the end of the form,
  with a one-line hint (wallpaper, clock and media controls), so the second half of the page is findable. Sub-page title
  "Appearance" -> "Lock Screen Appearance" (the header says which appearance).
- Order by use: untitled first section = Lock screen automatically, Delay before password required (moved up under the
  combo it depends on), Lock after waking from sleep; then "Manual Lock" (Keyboard shortcut). The blank spacer item is gone.
- New hint under the delay combo: "Time after locking during which the screen unlocks without a password."
- Labels kept (they are already sentence case with colons). Wallpaper type combo got an Accessible.name.
- Markers: LockOnResume, shortcut, ConfigureAppearance, wallpaperPluginId and the weak rows (custom duration dialogs, legacy
  Lock key). Relabel: inventory/relabel/kcm_screenlocker.tsv. Inventory --strict: 14 ok, 0 lost.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-013, HIG-019, HIG-057. Page-design 2, 3, 4.

Speed cause (code): kcm.cpp load() ran AppearanceSettings::load() before the first frame: KPackage lookup of the Plasma shell,
lock screen config.xml, wallpaper plugin config.xml, KConfigLoader and the property maps (kcm.cpp:49-53, appearancesettings.cpp
load/loadShellConfig/loadWallpaperConfig), none of which the main page uses. Now it runs in a QTimer::singleShot(0) after the
rest of load() (generation counter drops stale runs); AppearanceSettings getters and save() already null-check. The
KScreenSaverSettings constructor also scanned every Plasma/Wallpaper package; that list is only read by the Appearance page,
so it is now built on first call. Not changed: the settings store constructor (KGlobalAccel setShortcut/shortcut for the lock
action, kscreensaversettings.cpp store class) may block on kglobalacceld; it feeds the shortcut row on the main page, left as is.
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet. Unconfirmed without a build: that shellConfigFile/wallpaperConfigFile
(CONSTANT / NOTIFY properties) read correctly when the Appearance page is pushed after the deferred load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
